  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Trust Fund-Hunger Safety Net Programme (HSNP 3)- International Climate Funds (ICF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce poverty, hunger and vulnerability by providing 133,000 of the poorest households (approximately 798,000 people) in Kenya&apos;s arid and semi-arid lands with cash transfers and up to an additional 750,000 households (approximately 4,500,000 people) during drought emergencies. In addition, this final phase of the programme will ensure a transition of the Hunger Safety Net Programme to full Government of Kenya ownership and financing to guarantee the sustainability of the programme after a UK exit.</narrative>
  </description>
